Third-party material

Software dependencies are listed in WEB-Cargo.lock and CLI-Cargo.lock.
CLI-THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt and WEB-THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt retain
notices for their respective dependency sets. The web notices also include egui
embedded fonts (Hack, Ubuntu, Noto Emoji and emoji-icon-font), under the
license texts included there, including the Ubuntu Font Licence.
One is under a weak-copyleft licence: the acadrust
crate (DWG reading and writing, https://github.com/hakanaktt/acadrust) is licensed under the
Mozilla Public License 2.0 and is used unmodified as a separate library (crates/dwg). Its source
is available from crates.io and the repository above.


The core CADCraft assets are original (icons, drafting font, hatch patterns and
linetypes are drawn or defined in code). The per-file lists are in
WEB-ATTRIBUTION.md and CLI-ATTRIBUTION.md. Builds made with
the optional craft-fonts input (CRAFT_FONTS_DIR) embed the fonts listed in its ATTRIBUTION.md,
each under the SIL Open Font License 1.1; CRAFT-FONTS-ATTRIBUTION.md and
the included *-OFL.txt files retain their notices.
The web build embeds BIZ UDPGothic Regular, Noto Sans Arabic and NanumGothic.
The unmodified upstream CLI embeds Shippori Mincho Regular, BIZ UDPGothic Regular
and Bold, BIZ UDMincho Regular, Noto Sans Arabic and Noto Sans Thai.
Neither binary embeds the excluded Noto Sans CJK SC font.

StationDesk distribution provenance and source/build instructions: ../web-bundle/README.md.
The web build uses CADCraft e707ab4d7cc10102e550ad4c5bcecef1084a9baa.
The CLI is extracted without modification from the upstream v0.6.2 Linux x86_64
.deb (source 00c7613f1af3c73f7157fa91d9fe2635c6f23c06); it is not a StationDesk build.
Its unmodified MPL-2.0 acadrust 0.6.3 source is available at
https://crates.io/crates/acadrust/0.6.3 and
https://static.crates.io/crates/acadrust/acadrust-0.6.3.crate.
The web source lock uses acadrust 0.6.4:
https://static.crates.io/crates/acadrust/acadrust-0.6.4.crate.

